That rule makes the weapon-fusion system much more tactical. By locking a sword’s active moveset strictly to its forged elemental profile, a weapon's identity dictates its exact close-range and 5-meter ranged arsenal.
Here is how the Strict Elemental Matching Framework works, illustrated using your Lava + Acid + Fire + Dark Quad-Affinity Sword as the master blueprint.
System Rule: Strict Affinity Alignment
 * Affinity Lock: A weapon can ONLY execute elemental slashes, projectile arcs, and status conditions that directly belong to its forged elemental recipe.
 * Pure vs. Hybrid Scaling: Single-element swords hit with maximum focus in one status. Multi-element swords (like Quad-Affinity) split their damage types, applying multiple layered status effects at once.
 * Range Rule: Every valid element on the blade contributes both to its close-range contact strike and its 5-meter projectile arc slash.
Example Blueprint: The Lava-Acid-Fire-Dark Blade
Since this sword is forged with [Fire + Earth (Lava)] + [Acid] + [Fire] + [Dark], its entire moveset—both close-quarters physical hits and 5m projectile arcs—is restricted exclusively to those four intersecting affinities.
